    <ferc:ControlOverRespondentTextBlock id="f-1234" contextRef="c-12">&lt;p&gt;The Company is wholly owned by SIH, which is a wholly owned subsidiary of Startrans I, Inc. Startrans I, Inc is a wholly owned subsidiary of Starmeads I, LLC (formerly known as Startrans I, LLC). Starmeads I, LLC is a wholly owned subsidiary of Meads Investment Holdings, LLC an affiliate of the General Partner of Lotus Predecessor Fund I, LP (formerly known as Starwood Energy Infrastructure Fund, LP) and Lotus Predecessor Co-Invest Fund I, LP (formerly known as Starwood Energy Infrastructure Co-Invest Fund, LP)&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:ControlOverRespondentTextBlock>
    <ferc:NameOfCompanyControlledByRespondent id="f-1236" contextRef="c-304">-</ferc:NameOfCompanyControlledByRespondent>
    <ferc:OrderNumber id="f-1237" contextRef="c-304" unitRef="u-05" decimals="0">1</ferc:OrderNumber>
    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-1239" contextRef="c-12">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;1)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6)On July 31, 2025, ERSTE Abwicklungsanstalt assigned the Company's existing term loan to Associated Bank, N.A. (&amp;quot;Associated Bank&amp;quot;) and Associated Bank became the sole lender and administrative agent under the previously existing credit agreement. On July 31, 2025, the Company entered into an Amended and Restated Credit Agreement (&amp;quot;the Amended and Restated Credit Agreement&amp;quot;) with Associated Bank, as the Lender and Administrative Agent and refinanced its existing $2.31 million term loan and added an additional $2.0 Million term loan to rebalance the Company's capital structure, resulting in a $4.31 million senior secured term loan (the &amp;quot;Term Loan&amp;quot;). The Amended and Restated Credit Agreement extended the maturity date for the Term Loan to July 31, 2030 and requires quarterly payments of principal and interest as set forth in a new amortization schedule. In connection with the Amended and Restated Credit Agreement, the previously required debt equity ratio covenants and exit fee were removed; however, certain minimum debt ratios are required for distributions from the Company.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The debt is collateralized by all the Company's assets, including its transmission assets, and has a variable interest rate based on Adjusted Daily Compounded SOFR plus 2.75%. On August 7, 2025, the Company entered an interest rate swap transaction with Associated Bank on the $4.31 million Term Loan, converting the variable rate debt to fixed rate debt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The FERC issued an order dated May 9, 2025, authorizing the Company's request to increase its total debt by an additional $2.0 million in the Company's Section 204 filing in Docket No ES25-35-000.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;7)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;8)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;9)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;10)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;11)reserved&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;12)Refer to Footnote 4 in the Financial Notes - Rate Case - regarding the new rate case filing in Docket No. ER26-302 and requested changes to the Transmission Revenue Requirement (TRR) rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;13)E.A. Kratzman retired as Chief Executive Officer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;14)none&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
